# Normalize line endings to LF everywhere.
#
# Not cosmetic. The released stimulus set records a SHA-256 of its own contents, and
# git's autocrlf would hand a Windows clone CRLF bytes that no longer match that hash --
# so the same released artifact would fail its own integrity check depending on who
# cloned it. Pinning LF keeps the bytes identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Released data artifacts: byte-exact, never touched.
stimuli/** -text
*.jsonl -text

# Large binaries git should not try to diff or convert.
*.hdf5 binary
*.h5 binary
*.safetensors binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
